# What must NEVER reach forgelegacy.app. Gitignore syntax, read by wrangler at deploy time.
#
# ⚠ The 4 MB design-tool export. It is git-ignored, so it is present on every machine that has ever
# opened this folder and tracked by nothing — exactly the shape of file that gets published by accident.
# Uploaded, it becomes a public indexable page at /_exported-bundle.html whose <title> is "Bundled Page"
# and whose entire body lives inside a JavaScript string. The live site serves it as 404. Keep it that way.
_exported-bundle.html

# Repo documentation, not a page.
README.md
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore

# ⚠ WRANGLER'S OWN SCRATCH DIRECTORY, AND IT CAUGHT US ON THE FIRST RUN.
#
# `wrangler versions upload` writes a temp entrypoint to `.wrangler/tmp/deploy-XXXXXX/no-op-worker.js`
# — INSIDE the assets directory it is about to walk. So the very act of deploying created two files
# that were then published as site content: `/.wrangler/tmp/deploy-MNeLP3/no-op-worker.js` and its
# source map, both live public paths. Harmless in content, wrong in principle, and invisible in any
# check that reads the working tree rather than the upload manifest.
#
# The name is random per run, so this cannot be caught by listing files beforehand — only by reading
# what the upload actually said it sent. Read the manifest, not the directory.
.wrangler/
